# kernel: the kernel and the crates only it links. Debian's linux-image.
#
# Milestone 611 (every program and crate belongs to a package). The package's name, kind, home
# and membership are provisional, the lane's proposal for calef to ratify; the format is
# helpers/packages.py's header, and notes/package-boundaries.md has the table and the reasons.

name kernel
kind base
home kernel provisional

crate kernel
crate capability
crate paging
crate page_frames
crate pci
crate address_space_identifier
crate cpu_set
crate generational_table
crate inter_process_communication
crate intrusive_fifo
crate memory_corruption_canary_gate
crate memory_regions
crate thread_wake_handshake
crate work_steal_slot
crate direct_memory_access_validator
crate firmware_configuration
crate jh7110_clock_and_reset

exception 2026-09-27 kernel video_terminal kernel/src/user/ display tests and service wiring; pull request #1392 moves them
exception 2026-09-27 kernel non_volatile_memory_express the kernel hands the driver non_volatile_memory_express::Handoff, a contract living in a driver crate
exception 2026-09-27 kernel jh7110_entropy the kernel discovers the TRNG with the driver's own discover(); a board description living in a driver crate
exception 2026-09-27 kernel coremark the bench feature runs coremark inside the kernel; a benchmark is a fixture a release kernel should not link
exception 2026-09-27 kernel job_mix the kernel runs the job mix at boot; a fixture a release kernel should not link
exception 2026-09-27 kernel soak_page the soak and stack-depth probes; a fixture a release kernel should not link
